# Project-root .vercelignore for the Pathfinder Vercel project.
#
# Empty by design. Vercel reads this in preference to the repo-root
# `.vercelignore` (which excludes `Pathfinder/` so the parent
# `unicron-systems` Vercel project doesn't try to deploy it). Without
# this file, Vercel falls back to the repo-root one and strips the
# entire Pathfinder source tree before the build runs — package.json
# disappears and `next build` fails with "No Next.js version detected".
#
# Don't add exclusions here without confirming both:
#   1. They wouldn't be auto-stripped by Next.js's default bundling
#      (test files, .md files, .gitignore'd dirs already aren't bundled).
#   2. The corresponding entry isn't already in the repo-root
#      `.vercelignore` covering the parent project.
